    "done_when": "Reconcile the host and device moment coupling paths, as followup f-cfs-moment-path-reconcile on converged-forward-solve states, under the lead's decision resolution-strategy = refine-with-right-support (2026-10-10).\n\nMeasured by cfs-coupling-build-scale (H200 job 1283232, logs under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261010T184700018486-cfs-coupling-build-scale/logs): the device-batched coupling build differs from the host builder by 1.37e-7 norm-relative on the uniform channel and by 1.05e-3 (radial) and 1.55e-4 (vertical) on the moment channels at 550 cells, falling to 4.2e-9, 6.6e-5 and 1.1e-5 at 2,000. The certificate map still agrees within 1e-11. The worker traced the difference to the packed moments kernel's horizontally reflected edge pairing in nova/biot/polygonanalytic.py (pad_batch, _reflection_geometry, tile_evaluator with kernel=\"moments\").\n\nDone when:\n(1) An independent reference decides which path is correct. Use a dense high-order quadrature of the moment integrals, or a 50-digit mpmath evaluation on a sample of at least 200 source-target pairs drawn from the largest-difference entries and a random spread over the 550-cell certificate machine. Print per channel the maximum norm-relative and elementwise error of each path against the reference.\n(2) Repair the wrong path in nova/biot/polygonanalytic.py, with the moment reference point and accumulation order stated in the docstring in terms of what the moments are. After the repair, both paths agree within 1e-12 norm-relative on every block at 550 and 2,000 cells, and both agree with the reference within 1e-12.\n(3) If the host path is the wrong one, stop and report blocked before changing it. The host builder feeds every certified carrier, so its change needs the lead.\n(4) Negative control: restoring the unrepaired path brings back the measured norm-relative gap at 550 cells, by test id.\n(5) The tests covering polygonanalytic.py under tests/biot pass by delta on the H200 lane, run module by module as fresh processes with per-test timeouts. Add a new tests/biot/test_moment_path_parity.py carrying rows (2) and (4) at small cell counts.\n(6) Write an evidence fragment, docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-moment-path-reconcile.html, with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve and the reference table; reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.\n\nDo not edit nova/equilibrium or scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures, which other nodes own. You may import scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/coupling_build.py read-only from its merge, or from the run worktree /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/.reckon-worktrees/nova-a0f1e0938fc2/s21-nova/cfs-coupling-build-scale.\n\nRun conditions:\n- Run H200 work as one job, through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or as one sbatch job on betelgeuse with reservation gpu_0003_grpA. Set XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp. Submit for real and read squeue a minute later.\n- On a compute node, run the shared interpreter directly with PYTHONPATH set to the worktree, and never invoke uv there. Every login-node uv command carries --no-sync, and nothing runs uv sync.\n- Call configure_dtypes() before building any array, and assert jax_enable_x64.\n- Declare any wait as JSON-list wait_probe and wait_terminal on the job that finishes last.\n- Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step, writing the manifest before every wait. Status is complete, blocked or failed.",
